openmediavault-qnapx39 (7.4.0) stable; urgency=low

  * System > QNAP > Buttons: USB Copy (GP16) runs a chosen Scheduled
    Task, with the USB LED blinking while it runs; Reset (GP17) held 3 to
    10 seconds runs another. Adapted from openmediavault-qnap.
  * QTS beeps on the PC speaker: start-up, Reset, a stopped fan every
    5 minutes, a RAID degraded or rebuilding, a failed USB Copy.
  * QNAP device widget: model, serial number and BIOS from DMI.

 -- Rui <zrcz180@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:40:00 -0000

openmediavault-qnapx39 (7.3.0) stable; urgency=low

  * Fault emails through OMV notifications (System > Notification >
    Events, "QNAP TS-x39 hardware"): a failed fan, a critical temperature,
    a failed disk, a degraded RAID or a full volume (95 %) that lasts a
    minute, when it clears, and when the service stops unexpectedly.
  * System > QNAP > Disks: each bay with its disk, model, size,
    temperature, state and red LED.
  * Dashboard: fans and temperatures grid, device facts and history
    graphs of temperatures and fan speeds.
  * A critical temperature or a full volume also turns the Status LED red.

